# 0041-no-interrupt-handler-while-interrupts-disabled: the scheduler starts no interrupt handler (and ends
# no time slice) while the running context has interrupts disabled
#
# What it fixes: the game stops in several places (an idle title, the title with sound, a fight with
# inputs; docs/journal/011, 026) with its GS packet queue holding one entry that nothing sends. The game
# sends a packet inside DI ... EI (FUN_002D46B8: DI, wait for Status bit 16 to read clear, call
# FUN_002D3A60(-1), EI): the call stores the DMA channel's control register, which here finishes the
# transfer at once and queues the end-of-transfer interrupt, and only AFTER the store sets the "busy"
# counter. On the console the interrupt cannot arrive inside the section. Here the scheduler never read
# the status register, so the handler (FUN_002D3A60 with argument 1 or 2) could start at a checkpoint
# inside the section, find the counter still zero, return, and the game then marked the queue busy for an
# interrupt that never comes: the main thread spins in FUN_002D46B8 for ever.
#
# The change (EeScheduler): the head of the pending-invocation queue is not started while it is an
# interrupt (INTC/DMAC handler, alarm, GS callback) and the context it would interrupt has Status.EIE
# (bit 16, what the recompiled DI/EI clear and set), Status.IE (bit 0), or Status.EXL/ERL (bits 1, 2)
# not in the "enabled" state. It stays queued, in order (only the head is looked at, nothing is reordered,
# nothing is dropped or duplicated), and m_interruptsDeferred makes the slow path look at it again every
# kInterruptRecheckCycles (64 EE cycles, 8 dispatches) until the context enables interrupts: after an EI
# nothing calls the scheduler, so the fast path alone would wait for the next IOP batch (256 dispatches).
# The end of the time slice (the console's timer interrupt) is postponed the same way. RPC, SIF command,
# syscall-override, exit-handler and HLE invocations are the runtime's own calls and are not gated. The
# idle path (no thread running) has no context to be disabled and is not gated.
#
# Not changed (one topic per patch): a cause that arrives while its mask or handler is not enabled is
# still dropped instead of staying pending (journal 011).
#
# Verified: tests/runtime/irq_di_section_test.cpp (300 rounds of DI; raise the DMAC channel-1 interrupt;
# 40 small calls; mark busy; EI): unpatched the handler starts inside the section in 300 of 300 rounds and
# busy is never cleared; patched 0 of 300, every interrupt delivered once. pacing_neutral_test and
# scheduler_fast_path_test pass.
#
diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ee_scheduler.h b/ps2xRuntime/include/runtime/ee_scheduler.h
index 13a5776..9a8ba4b 100644
